@startuml
title L2-037 - Local credential sign-in
actor Photographer
participant "Sign-in page" as page
participant SessionService as client
participant "API / request protection" as api
participant SignInCommandHandler as handler
participant "PasswordService / JwtService" as crypto
database PostgreSQL as db
Photographer -> page : Enter email and password
page -> client : signIn(credentials)
client -> api : GET /api/session/csrf
api --> client : Antiforgery cookie and header
client -> api : POST /api/session/sign-in with proof
api -> api : Validate origin, antiforgery, IP budget
api -> handler : MediatR SignInCommand
handler -> db : Find normalized email
handler -> crypto : Verify password (dummy hash if unknown)
alt Invalid credentials
handler --> api : Generic 401
api --> client : Safe error
client --> page : Clear password; retain email
else Valid credentials
handler -> crypto : Sign JWT
handler -> db : Revoke previous session; save new token hash
handler --> api : Session result and internal JWT
api --> client : Session JSON; Secure HttpOnly JWT cookie
client -> api : GET /api/session
api --> client : Current session and identity-bound antiforgery proof
client --> page : Update signal; navigate to local destination
end
note over api,db
Each authenticated request validates JWT and database session.
Sign-out removes session; password reset revokes all user sessions.
Reject at 30 minutes idle or exactly 12 hours absolute.
end note
@enduml
